From f35f140fb556ee6d4ae23b88391fcd9c9997a7d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drama-agent <agent@plotarmor.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:58:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drama3 metal: eos in every nucleus, a serve silence default
 and a redraw of a silenced take

After the speech the model wants to end, one token can hold ~96.6% of the
candidate mass with eos rank 1 at 2-22%, so eos's cumulative probability
exceeds both top_p cutoffs (0.9 request draw, 0.95 RAS redraw) and both
truncated draws exclude the stop every frame; the take runs to the frame
cap. Keep the eos candidate slot in every nucleus of both main-token draws
(test-drama-sampler-device runs the shader's rule on the GPU) and fill an
unset Drama guard at -40 dBFS / 3.5 s, validated after the fill, to end the
trailing quiet the same collapse produces; --silence-seconds 0 disables it.

On the int3 build that collapse can also come mid-text: the pause token
takes the mass after a sentence and the take ends in silence with the rest
unspoken. It is a per-seed degeneracy (5 of 8 medium-05 seeds speak the
whole text and stop), so serve redraws a silenced buffered Drama take up
to twice with the next prompt-derived seed; --silence-redraws 0 keeps the
first take. Takes the guard never trips are untouched, byte for byte.

drama3-generate --logits-out FILE dumps each frame's candidate-head logits
for results/smaller-builds/trace_eos.py.
